// The Electron build of the light theme.
//
// `renderer.nim`'s `loadTheme` resolves the configured theme to
// `frontend/styles/{name}_theme_electron.css`, so a config carrying
// `theme: "default_white"` asks for THIS file by name. Until it existed the
// href resolved to nothing, the `#theme` link went dead and the window
// rendered as unstyled HTML — which is why the light theme could not be
// screenshotted, reviewed or shipped.
//
// It is deliberately the same three lines as
// `default_dark_theme_electron.styl`, differing only in which palette is
// imported: the palette files carry every colour, and `codetracer.styl`
// carries every rule. Any divergence in structure between the two entry
// points would mean the light build is a different stylesheet rather than the
// same stylesheet in a different palette.
@import "default_white_theme"
IS_EXTENSION = false
@import "codetracer"
